From 74deef7b8774724f4d17d8799a2a72667e4a4f63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:22:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(installer): tell an APK from a bundle by its content,
 not its suffix

PackageBundles.isBundle decided by the file name alone (.apks, .xapk,
.apkm, .apk+). A single APK that a download site saved as .xapk was then
unpacked as an archive, found no .apk entry and failed with "No base APK",
and a ZIP of APKs saved as .apk went to the APK parser and failed there.
The icon handler's IconApks made the same choice.

Decide by content instead, as the package parser itself does: an APK is a
ZIP with AndroidManifest.xml at its root; a bundle has none there and holds
.apk entries. A file that is not a ZIP is not a bundle, so the APK parser
reports it as before.

tests/package/PackageBundlesTest.java runs the production class on real
ZIP files (tools/test_package_bundles.py, in its own small workflow as the
application storage contracts are). SplitPackageContractTest installs a
base APK saved as .xapk, and IconBundleTest reads an APK named .xapk and a
bundle named .apk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
